quran[10]{c,v,t}:
  28,85,"Indeed, the One Who has ordained the Qur’an for you will surely bring you back to the place of return (i.e. Mecca). Say: ‘My Lord knows best who has come with guidance and who is in manifest error.’"
  28,86,You did not hope that the Book would be delivered to you. But it was a mercy from your Lord. So do not ever be an advocate of the disbelievers (to protect them from My torment).
  28,87,"Do not ever let them bar you from (conveying) Allah’s revelations after they have been sent down to you. Invite (all) to (the way of) your Lord, and never be among the polytheists."
  28,88,"And do not worship another god besides Allah. There is no god except Him. Everything is bound to perish except Him (i.e. His Pre-Eternal Being). All authority belongs to Him, and to Him, you (all) shall be returned."
  29,1,"Alif, Lam, Mim."
  29,2,"Do people think they will be left once they say, ‘We believe,’ and they will not be tried?"
  29,3,"Indeed, We tested those before them. So Allah shall surely distinguish those who are truthful and expose the liars."
  29,4,Do those who commit evil deeds think they will surpass Us? Evil indeed is the judgement they make!
  29,5,"Whoever hopes to meet Allah (should know that) Allah’s appointed time will indeed come. And He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing."
  29,6,"Whosoever strives hard (in Allah’s cause) strives only for his own sake. Indeed, Allah is Self-Sufficient (and not in need) of (His) creation."
